          <p class="dt-caption" id="feedCap"><span class="lang-en">Huginn starts the loop from
            <b>random noise</b>: s₀ ~ N(0, σ²I), σ² = 2/5 — not zeros, not the embedding. The input
            only ever arrives through the injection junction, and the trained model is
            path-independent: the loop converges toward an input-conditioned fixed point regardless
            of s₀.</span><span class="lang-ko">Huginn은 loop를 <b>random noise</b>에서 시작한다:
            s₀ ~ N(0, σ²I), σ² = 2/5 — zero도 embedding도 아니다. 입력은 오직 injection junction을
            통해서만 들어오고, 학습된 모델은 path-independent해서 s₀가 무엇이든 입력-조건부 fixed
            point로 수렴한다.</span></p>

          <noscript>
            <p class="viz-sub">
              <span class="lang-en">With JavaScript this panel steps one token through the loop and
                redraws the wiring for all four variants. The static view shows Huginn’s wiring:
                noise init s₀, concat-adapter injection A·[sᵢ₋₁; e] at every iteration, one
                weight-tied 4-layer core, coda on the final state.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">JavaScript가 있으면 이 패널은 token 하나를 loop에 한 스텝씩
                통과시키고 4개 variant의 배선을 다시 그린다. 정적 뷰는 Huginn의 배선이다: noise
                init s₀, 매 iteration의 concat-adapter 주입 A·[sᵢ₋₁; e], weight-tied 4-layer core
                하나, 마지막 state에 대한 coda.</span>
            </p>
          </noscript>
        </div>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">The three verified injection mechanisms — concat + adapter
            (Huginn), decay-SSM (Parcae), additive E + h (LOTUS) — are three answers to the same
            question, and the public Parcae repo ships all three as selectable modules
            (<code>LinearInjection</code>, <code>DiagonalInjection</code>,
            <code>AdditiveInjection</code> in <code>parcae_lm/modules/injection.py</code>). Even
            the initial state is deliberate: noise, so the model learns to converge from
            anywhere.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">검증된 세 가지 주입 메커니즘 — concat + adapter(Huginn),
            decay-SSM(Parcae), additive E + h(LOTUS) — 은 같은 질문에 대한 세 가지 답이고, 공개
            Parcae repo는 셋 다 선택 가능한 모듈로 제공한다
            (<code>parcae_lm/modules/injection.py</code>의 <code>LinearInjection</code>,
            <code>DiagonalInjection</code>, <code>AdditiveInjection</code>). 초기 state까지도
            의도적이다: noise에서 시작해, 어디서 출발하든 수렴하도록 학습시킨다.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">A working looped LM computes sᵢ = R(e, sᵢ₋₁), not hᵢ = f(hᵢ₋₁):
            the input is re-injected at every iteration and the state starts from noise — with e
            only at the start, “the iterative process would not be stable” (Huginn §3.1).</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">작동하는 looped LM은 hᵢ = f(hᵢ₋₁)이 아니라 sᵢ = R(e, sᵢ₋₁)을
            계산한다: 입력이 매 iteration 재주입되고 state는 noise에서 출발한다 — e가 시작에만
            주어지면 “iterative process는 불안정하다” (Huginn §3.1).</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">Re-injection feeds the loop — but what guarantees that 32 passes of the same block contract instead of exploding?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">재주입이 loop를 먹여 살린다 — 그런데 같은 block을 32번 통과시켜도 폭발하지 않고 수축한다는 보장은 어디서 오는가?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §5 · STABILITY ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s5">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="arc-heading"><span class="arc-num">§5</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Keeping the loop stable: ρ(Ā) decides</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">Loop 안정화: ρ(Ā)가 결정한다</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">Here §2’s fixed-point dichotomy becomes measurable. Iterate a map,
            and the spectral radius of its transition decides everything: below 1, contraction to a
            fixed point; at or above 1, explosion. Parcae located exactly this quantity inside
            trained looped LMs.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">§2의 fixed-point 이분법이 여기서 측정 가능한 것이 된다. map을
            반복하면 transition의 spectral radius가 모든 것을 결정한다: 1 미만이면 fixed point로
            수축, 1 이상이면 폭발. Parcae는 바로 이 양을 학습된 looped LM 안에서 찾아냈다.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Parcae’s diagnosis of why looped-LM training blows up: divergent
            runs learn a spectral radius ρ(Ā) ≥ 1 in the injection parameters; convergent runs keep
            ρ(Ā) &lt; 1. Drag the slider across the boundary.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">looped-LM 학습이 폭발하는 이유에 대한 Parcae의 진단: 발산하는
            run은 injection 파라미터에서 spectral radius ρ(Ā) ≥ 1을 학습하고, 수렴하는 run은
            ρ(Ā) &lt; 1을 유지한다. slider를 경계 너머로 움직여 보자.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="eq-chips">
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="The loop update, as Parcae models it: the injection transition Ā decays the state, B̄ injects the input, and R̄ is the transformer block’s residual contribution." data-tip-ko="Parcae가 모델링한 loop 업데이트: injection transition Ā가 state를 감쇠시키고, B̄가 입력을 주입하며, R̄는 transformer block의 residual 기여분이다.">h<sub>t+1</sub> = Ā·h<sub>t</sub> + B̄·e + R̄(h<sub>t</sub>, e)</span>
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="The structural fix: parameterize A = Diag(−exp(log_A)) and discretize (ZOH) with a learnable Δ, so Ā = exp(ΔA) has spectral radius < 1 by construction — every diagonal decay entry lands in (0, 1)." data-tip-ko="구조적 해결책: A = Diag(−exp(log_A))로 파라미터화하고 learnable Δ로 (ZOH) 이산화하면 Ā = exp(ΔA)의 spectral radius가 구조적으로 1 미만 — 대각 decay 성분 전부가 (0, 1)에 들어간다.">Ā = exp(Δ·A), A = Diag(−exp(log_A)) → ρ(Ā) &lt; 1</span>
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="Verbatim from the public repo, SandyResearch/parcae parcae_lm/modules/injection.py (DiagonalInjection docstring): x_{t+1} = exp(−dt·A)·x_t + dt·B@e, with dt = softplus(dt_bias), A = exp(A_log), B identity-initialized. A helper get_spectral_norm() returns decay.max()." data-tip-ko="Public repo 원문 — SandyResearch/parcae의 parcae_lm/modules/injection.py (DiagonalInjection docstring): x_{t+1} = exp(−dt·A)·x_t + dt·B@e, dt = softplus(dt_bias), A = exp(A_log), B는 identity 초기화. get_spectral_norm() 헬퍼가 decay.max()를 반환한다.">code: x·e^(−dt·A) + dt·B@e — injection.py</span>
          </div>

          <div class="loop-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 740 360" role="img" aria-label="State norm over loop iterations: two initializations contracting to the same fixed point when the spectral radius is below one, versus residual state explosion when it is at least one" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:680px;">
            <line x1="70" y1="300" x2="700" y2="300" stroke="#d1cfc5" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
            <line x1="70" y1="50" x2="70" y2="300" stroke="#d1cfc5" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
            <text class="mlabel" x="385" y="336" text-anchor="middle">loop iteration t</text>
            <text class="mlabel" x="26" y="175" transform="rotate(-90 26 175)" text-anchor="middle">‖state‖ (schematic)</text>
            {[0, 6, 12, 18, 24].map((t) => (
              <text class="mlabel" x={stabX(t)} y="316" text-anchor="middle">{t}</text>
            ))}

            <line x1="70" y1={FP_Y} x2="700" y2={FP_Y} stroke="#b9b7ad" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 5"></line>
            <text class="mlabel" x="696" y={FP_Y - 7} text-anchor="end">input-conditioned fixed point h*</text>

            <g data-tip="ρ = 0.8, two different initializations — one far above the fixed point, one near zero — converging to the SAME h*. This is Huginn’s path independence (in the sense of Anil et al. 2022): the trained loop’s destination is set by the input e, not by s₀." data-tip-ko="ρ = 0.8, 서로 다른 두 초기화 — 하나는 fixed point 위쪽 멀리, 하나는 0 근처 — 가 같은 h*로 수렴한다. Huginn의 path independence(Anil et al. 2022의 의미)가 이것이다: 학습된 loop의 종착지는 s₀가 아니라 입력 e가 정한다.">
              <polyline class="curve-conv" points={PTS_CONV_A}></polyline>
              <polyline class="curve-conv" points={PTS_CONV_B}></polyline>
            </g>
            <g data-tip="ρ = 1.05: the state norm compounds every iteration — Parcae’s “residual state explosion and loss spikes”. Divergent training runs are the ones that learned ρ(Ā) ≥ 1." data-tip-ko="ρ = 1.05: state norm이 매 iteration 복리로 커진다 — Parcae가 말한 “residual state explosion과 loss spike”. 발산한 학습 run들이 바로 ρ(Ā) ≥ 1을 학습한 run들이다.">
              <polyline class="curve-div" points={PTS_DIV}></polyline>
            </g>
            <polyline id="trajUser" class="curve-user" points={PTS_USER}></polyline>

            <g transform="translate(90, 58)">
              <line class="curve-conv" x1="0" y1="0" x2="26" y2="0"></line>
              <text class="ssub" x="32" y="4">ρ = 0.8 — two inits, one fixed point (path independence)</text>
              <line class="curve-div" x1="0" y1="18" x2="26" y2="18"></line>
              <text class="ssub" x="32" y="22">ρ = 1.05 — residual state explosion</text>
              <line class="curve-user" x1="0" y1="36" x2="26" y2="36"></line>
              <text class="ssub" x="32" y="40">your ρ (slider)</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="slider-row">
            <span class="smono slider-lbl">ρ(Ā)</span>
            <input type="range" id="rhoSlider" min="70" max="110" value="95" aria-label="Spectral radius of the state transition" />
            <span class="smono" id="rhoVal">0.95</span>
          </div>

          <p class="dt-caption" id="stabCap"><span class="lang-en">ρ = 0.95: still contracting,
            just slowly — the state closes most of the distance to its fixed point within ~20
            iterations. Parcae makes this regime <b>structural</b>: the diagonal decay
            e^(−Δ·A) is elementwise in (0, 1) by construction, so the injection transition cannot
            learn its way past ρ = 1.</span><span class="lang-ko">ρ = 0.95: 여전히 수축하지만
            느리다 — state는 ~20 iteration 안에 fixed point까지 거리 대부분을 좁힌다. Parcae는 이
            영역을 <b>구조적으로</b> 보장한다: 대각 decay e^(−Δ·A)가 구조상 elementwise로 (0, 1)에
            있으므로, injection transition은 학습으로도 ρ = 1을 넘을 수 없다.</span></p>

          <p class="fine-note">
            <span class="lang-en"><b>Precision note.</b> The ρ(Ā) &lt; 1 guarantee covers the
              injection transition Ā only — the full loop map includes the transformer term
              R̄(h, e), so end-to-end stability is empirical (Parcae shows it tracks ρ(Ā) in
              practice). Huginn’s stability comes from a different pair: input re-injection every
              step + noise init, with convergence to input-conditioned fixed points verified
              post-training. Chart curves are a schematic scalar model x ← ρx + 1, not model
              traces.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko"><b>정밀 주석.</b> ρ(Ā) &lt; 1 보장은 injection transition Ā에만
              해당한다 — 전체 loop map에는 transformer 항 R̄(h, e)가 포함되므로 end-to-end 안정성은
              경험적이다 (Parcae는 실측에서 ρ(Ā)를 따라감을 보인다). Huginn의 안정성은 다른 조합에서
              온다: 매 스텝 입력 재주입 + noise init, 그리고 학습 후 검증된 입력-조건부 fixed
              point로의 수렴. 차트의 곡선은 x ← ρx + 1 스칼라 모형의 개략도이지 실제 모델 trace가
              아니다.</span>
          </p>

          <div class="eq-chips">
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="Parcae’s additional stabilizers beyond the diagonal injection: a normalization layer on the prelude output e (prelude_norm=True in shipped configs) and per-sequence depth sampling inside each batch to reduce loss spikes (recurrent_iteration_method='per-sequence')." data-tip-ko="대각 injection 외 Parcae의 추가 안정장치: prelude 출력 e에 대한 normalization (배포 config의 prelude_norm=True)과 loss spike를 줄이는 배치 내 per-sequence depth sampling (recurrent_iteration_method='per-sequence').">+ prelude output norm · per-sequence depth sampling (Parcae)</span>
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="Huginn maintains path independence in the sense of Anil et al. (2022): the state converges toward input-conditioned fixed points regardless of initialization — verified on the trained model." data-tip-ko="Huginn은 Anil et al. (2022) 의미의 path independence를 유지한다: state가 초기화와 무관하게 입력-조건부 fixed point로 수렴 — 학습된 모델에서 검증됨.">+ noise init → path independence (Huginn)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">Divergent training runs are the ones that learned ρ(Ā) ≥ 1 in the
            injection parameters; Parcae’s diagonal decay Ā = exp(ΔA) keeps every entry in (0, 1)
            by construction, so the injection transition cannot leave the contracting regime —
            stability becomes structural, not lucky.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">발산한 학습 run들은 injection 파라미터에서 ρ(Ā) ≥ 1을 학습해 버린
            run들이다; Parcae의 대각 decay Ā = exp(ΔA)는 구조적으로 모든 성분을 (0, 1)에 가두므로,
            injection transition은 수축 영역을 벗어날 수 없다 — 안정성이 운이 아니라 구조가 된다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">A stable loop still has to be trained at some depth. Which r do you unroll — and can you afford backprop through all of it?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">안정적인 loop라도 결국 어떤 깊이에서 학습되어야 한다. 어떤 r로 펼칠 것인가 — 그리고 그 전부를 backprop할 여력은 있는가?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §6 · TRAINING ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s6">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="arc-heading"><span class="arc-num">§6</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Training the loop: random depth, truncated gradients</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">Loop 학습: random depth와 truncated gradient</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">Stability makes deep unrolling possible; training decides which
            depths the model will ever be good at. Bake in one r and depth stops being a knob — so
            the working recipe makes r itself a random variable, and keeps the backprop bill
            bounded.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">안정성은 깊은 unrolling을 가능하게 하고, 학습은 모델이 어떤
            깊이에서 잘할지를 결정한다. r 하나를 구워 넣으면 깊이는 더 이상 노브가 아니다 — 그래서
            작동하는 레시피는 r 자체를 확률변수로 만들고, backprop 청구서는 유한하게 묶는다.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Three verified schemes. Depth is sampled per step so the model
            never overfits one loop count; gradients flow through only a suffix of the loop;
            and LOTUS adds dense supervision on the latent positions.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">검증된 세 가지 방식. depth를 스텝마다 샘플링해 모델이 특정 loop
            수에 과적합하지 않게 하고, gradient는 loop의 suffix로만 흘리며, LOTUS는 latent 위치에
            dense supervision을 더한다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <h3 class="panel-h">
            <span class="lang-en">6a · Depth is a random variable at train time</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">6a · 학습 시 depth는 확률변수다</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="panel-sub">
            <span class="lang-en">Huginn samples r per step from a log-normal Poisson:
              τ ~ N(log r̄ − ½σ², σ), r ~ Poisson(e^τ) + 1, with σ = ½ and mean recurrence
              r̄ = 32, over 800 B tokens. Parcae samples Poisson depths per sequence
              (repo: <code>poisson-truncated-full</code>). The histogram below is that exact
              Huginn distribution, computed numerically.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">Huginn은 스텝마다 log-normal Poisson에서 r을 뽑는다:
              τ ~ N(log r̄ − ½σ², σ), r ~ Poisson(e^τ) + 1, σ = ½, 평균 recurrence r̄ = 32,
              800 B token 학습. Parcae는 시퀀스별 Poisson depth를 샘플링한다
              (repo: <code>poisson-truncated-full</code>). 아래 히스토그램은 Huginn의 그 분포를
              수치적으로 계산한 것이다.</span>
          </p>
          <div class="loop-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 760 260" role="img" aria-label="Probability mass of the sampled loop count r under Huginn's log-normal Poisson depth distribution with mean 32" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:700px;">
            <g data-tip="P(r) under τ ~ N(log 32 − ⅛, ½), r ~ Poisson(e^τ) + 1 — computed by numerical integration over τ. Most mass sits near r̄ = 32, with a long right tail (clipped at r = 80): training regularly visits both shallow and very deep unrollings." data-tip-ko="τ ~ N(log 32 − ⅛, ½), r ~ Poisson(e^τ) + 1에서의 P(r) — τ에 대한 수치 적분으로 계산. 질량 대부분이 r̄ = 32 근처에 있고 오른쪽 꼬리가 길다 (r = 80에서 절단): 학습은 얕은 unrolling과 아주 깊은 unrolling을 모두 정기적으로 방문한다.">
              {depthBars.map((b) => (
                <rect class="pmf-bar" x={b.x} y={220 - b.h} width="6.4" height={Math.max(b.h, 0.5)} rx="1"></rect>
              ))}
            </g>
            <line x1="60" y1="220" x2="702" y2="220" stroke="#d1cfc5" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
            <line x1={60 + 31 * 8 + 3.2} y1="42" x2={60 + 31 * 8 + 3.2} y2="220" stroke="#141413" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4" opacity="0.6"></line>
            <text class="mlabel" x={60 + 31 * 8 + 10} y="52">mean recurrence r̄ = 32</text>
            {[1, 16, 32, 48, 64, 80].map((r) => (
              <text class="mlabel" x={60 + (r - 1) * 8 + 3.2} y="238" text-anchor="middle">{r}</text>
            ))}
            <text class="mlabel" x="385" y="256" text-anchor="middle">sampled loop count r — log-normal Poisson, σ = ½ (Huginn §3.3)</text>
          </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <h3 class="panel-h">
            <span class="lang-en">6b · Truncated backprop: gradients only through the last k</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">6b · Truncated backprop: 마지막 k개에만 gradient</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="panel-sub">
            <span class="lang-en">Unrolling 32+ iterations for backprop would be ruinous. Huginn
              backpropagates through only the <b>last k = 8</b> iterations — the earlier prefix runs
              under no-grad. Parcae’s repo implements the same two-phase loop (no-grad prefix,
              with-grad suffix) with μ_bwd = ⌈μ_rec/2⌉, e.g. 8 total / 4 backprop at 140M. LOTUS,
              with only R = 6, backprops through all of them.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">32+ iteration을 backprop용으로 전부 펼치면 비용이 파멸적이다.
              Huginn은 <b>마지막 k = 8</b> iteration만 backprop하고, 앞쪽 prefix는 no-grad로 돌린다.
              Parcae repo도 같은 2-phase loop(no-grad prefix, with-grad suffix)를 구현하며
              μ_bwd = ⌈μ_rec/2⌉ — 140M 기준 전체 8 / backprop 4. LOTUS는 R = 6뿐이라 전부
              backprop한다.</span>
          </p>
          <div class="dt-controls">
            <button class="btn ghost btn-sm" id="btnBptt" type="button">▶ Run backward pass</button>
            <span class="dt-step" id="bpttStep">forward: 16 iterations sampled</span>
          </div>
          <div class="loop-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 760 150" role="img" aria-label="Sixteen loop iterations: the first eight run under no-grad, gradients flow only through the last eight" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:700px;">
            {Array.from({ length: 16 }, (_, i) => (
              <g data-tip={i < 8
                ? `Iteration ${i + 1} — forward only, torch.no_grad(). Its activations are never stored for backprop; it only shapes the state the gradient window will start from.`
                : `Iteration ${i + 1} — inside the k = 8 gradient window: activations kept, gradients flow. (Huginn: “we backpropagate through only the last k iterations of the recurrent unit”.)`}
                 data-tip-ko={i < 8
                ? `Iteration ${i + 1} — forward만, torch.no_grad(). activation을 backprop용으로 저장하지 않는다; gradient window가 출발할 state를 만들어 줄 뿐이다.`
                : `Iteration ${i + 1} — k = 8 gradient window 안: activation 유지, gradient가 흐른다. (Huginn: “recurrent unit의 마지막 k개 iteration만 backprop한다”.)`}>
                <rect class={`bp-cell ${i < 8 ? 'bp-ng' : 'bp-g'}`} x={30 + i * 44} y="40" width="38" height="44" rx="7" data-i={i}></rect>
                <text class="mlabel" x={49 + i * 44} y="66" text-anchor="middle">{i + 1}</text>
