            <text class="ssub" x="206" y="26" text-anchor="middle">no-grad prefix — forward only</text>
            <text class="ssub bp-glbl" x="558" y="26" text-anchor="middle">gradient window — last k = 8</text>
            <path id="bpArrow" class="bp-arrow" d="M734,105 H382" marker-end="url(#arrLoop)"></path>
            <text class="smono" x="558" y="128" text-anchor="middle">∂L flows right → left, stops at the window edge</text>
            <text class="smono" x="206" y="128" text-anchor="middle">torch.no_grad()</text>
          </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <h3 class="panel-h">
            <span class="lang-en">6c · LOTUS: dense latent supervision — dense across positions, at the final iteration</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">6c · LOTUS: dense latent supervision — 위치에 대해 dense, 마지막 iteration에서</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="panel-sub">
            <span class="lang-en">Every latent position’s <b>post-loop</b> state h⁽ᴿ⁾ is decoded
              through the base LM head and scored against its gold CoT-step token — dense
              across the K × c = 150 positions, applied at iteration R (not per-iteration). Either
              loss alone collapses gold-step recovery to ~9% top-1; combined, 70.9% top-1 / 85.8%
              top-5.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">모든 latent 위치의 <b>loop 통과 후</b> state h⁽ᴿ⁾를 base
              LM head로 decode해 gold CoT-step token과 대조한다 — K × c = 150개 위치에 대해
              dense하고, iteration R에서 적용된다 (iteration마다가 아니다). 두 loss 중 하나만 쓰면
              gold-step 복원율이 ~9% top-1로 무너지고, 결합하면 70.9% top-1 / 85.8% top-5.</span>
          </p>
          <div class="loop-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 760 250" role="img" aria-label="LOTUS input layout: question, six blocks of 25 latent tokens, answer; each latent position's final-iteration state is decoded through the LM head against a gold chain-of-thought step token" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:700px;">
            <g data-tip="ℒ_step = mean CE over all K × c latent positions: each post-loop state hᵢⱼ⁽ᴿ⁾ decoded by the base LM head f_head against gold step token Tᵢⱼ." data-tip-ko="ℒ_step = 모든 K × c latent 위치에 대한 평균 CE: 각 loop 통과 후 state hᵢⱼ⁽ᴿ⁾를 base LM head f_head로 decode해 gold step token Tᵢⱼ와 대조.">
              <rect class="sbox sbox-accent" x="200" y="24" width="360" height="44" rx="9"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm taccent" x="380" y="43" text-anchor="middle">f_head — base LM head (readout)</text>
              <text class="smono" x="380" y="59" text-anchor="middle">CE( f_head(hᵢⱼ⁽ᴿ⁾), Tᵢⱼ ) — gold CoT step tokens</text>
            </g>
            {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((k) => (
              <line class="flowline-thin" x1={205 + k * 62 + 25} y1="112" x2={230 + (k - 2.5) * 40 + 150} y2="70" marker-end="url(#arrL)"></line>
            ))}

            <g data-tip="The question is processed once; its KV cache C_pre is reused by every loop iteration." data-tip-ko="question은 한 번만 처리되고, 그 KV cache C_pre를 모든 loop iteration이 재사용한다.">
              <rect class="sbox" x="20" y="114" width="120" height="46" rx="8"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm" x="80" y="134" text-anchor="middle">Q — question</text>
              <text class="smono" x="80" y="151" text-anchor="middle">→ C_pre, once</text>
            </g>
            <rect class="tok-chip" x="146" y="120" width="34" height="34" rx="6"></rect>
            <text class="mlabel" x="163" y="141" text-anchor="middle">BoT</text>
            {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((k) => (
              <g data-tip={`Latent block ${k + 1} of K = 6 — c = 25 ⟨lat⟩ tokens. Only these K × c positions are looped R = 6 times through the whole 3B backbone; each one is supervised against its gold CoT-step token at iteration R.`}
                 data-tip-ko={`Latent block ${k + 1} / K = 6 — c = 25개의 ⟨lat⟩ token. 이 K × c 위치들만 3B backbone 전체를 R = 6번 통과하며, 각 위치는 iteration R에서 gold CoT-step token으로 supervision된다.`}>
                <rect class="lat-chip" x={186 + k * 62} y="114" width="56" height="46" rx="8"></rect>
                <text class="stitle sm tlin" x={214 + k * 62} y="134" text-anchor="middle">lat {k + 1}</text>
                <text class="smono" x={214 + k * 62} y="151" text-anchor="middle">× 25</text>
              </g>
            ))}
            <rect class="tok-chip" x="562" y="120" width="34" height="34" rx="6"></rect>
            <text class="mlabel" x="579" y="141" text-anchor="middle">EoT</text>
            <g data-tip="ℒ_ans: standard CE on the answer tokens, from a final forward pass with the post-loop latents inserted." data-tip-ko="ℒ_ans: loop 통과 후 latent들을 삽입한 마지막 forward pass에서 answer token들에 대한 표준 CE.">
              <rect class="sbox" x="602" y="114" width="138" height="46" rx="8"></rect>
              <text class="stitle sm" x="671" y="134" text-anchor="middle">A — answer</text>
              <text class="smono" x="671" y="151" text-anchor="middle">ℒ_ans (CE)</text>
            </g>

            <text class="smono" x="380" y="196" text-anchor="middle">ℒ = ℒ_ans + λ_step · ℒ_step — full backprop through all R = 6 iterations</text>
            <text class="ssub" x="380" y="220" text-anchor="middle">ablation: either loss alone → ~9% gold-step top-1; combined → 70.9% top-1 / 85.8% top-5 (arXiv 2606.31779)</text>
          </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">Three verified tricks — sample r per step (log-normal Poisson,
            r̄ = 32), backprop only through the last k = 8 iterations, and (LOTUS) supervise every
            latent position at the final iteration — together produce a core that behaves at any
            r.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">검증된 세 가지 트릭 — r을 스텝마다 샘플링(log-normal Poisson,
            r̄ = 32), 마지막 k = 8 iteration만 backprop, 그리고 (LOTUS) 마지막 iteration에서 모든
            latent 위치를 supervision — 이 셋이 합쳐져 어떤 r에서도 제대로 동작하는 core를
            만든다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">Trained under random depth, the model accepts any r at inference. What does turning that knob actually buy — and when does it stop paying?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">random depth로 학습된 모델은 inference에서 어떤 r이든 받는다. 그 노브를 돌리면 실제로 무엇을 얻는가 — 그리고 언제부터 돈값을 못 하는가?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §7 · TEST-TIME DEPTH ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s7">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="arc-heading"><span class="arc-num">§7</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Test-time depth: the runtime knob, and what it caches</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">Test-time depth: 런타임 노브, 그리고 무엇이 cache되는가</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">This is the payoff the title promised. Because no single depth was
            baked in at training, r is now an inference-time choice — the interesting facts are the
            shape of the quality curve, and what each extra loop quietly costs.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">제목이 약속한 보상이 여기다. 학습에서 특정 깊이가 구워지지
            않았으므로 r은 이제 inference 시점의 선택이다 — 흥미로운 사실은 품질 곡선의 모양, 그리고
            추가 loop 하나하나가 조용히 청구하는 비용이다.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Trained under random r, the model accepts any r at inference.
            Quality follows a saturating exponential — Parcae fits it explicitly as
            ℒ(T) = ℒ<sub>∞</sub> + Z·e<sup>−zT</sup> — with task-dependent ceilings: Huginn reports
            HellaSwag near-saturating at ~8 recurrences while GSM8K keeps improving to r ≈ 32–64.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">random r로 학습된 모델은 inference에서 어떤 r이든 받는다. 품질은
            포화 지수 곡선을 따르고 — Parcae는 이를 ℒ(T) = ℒ<sub>∞</sub> + Z·e<sup>−zT</sup>로 명시적으로
            피팅한다 — 천장은 task마다 다르다: Huginn 보고 기준 HellaSwag은 recurrence ~8에서 거의
            포화하고 GSM8K는 r ≈ 32–64까지 계속 오른다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="loop-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 740 360" role="img" aria-label="Schematic quality versus loop count: a recall-style task saturating by about eight loops and a reasoning-style task still improving at sixty-four, with the KL-threshold early-exit point marked" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:680px;">
            <line x1="70" y1="300" x2="700" y2="300" stroke="#d1cfc5" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
            <line x1="70" y1="50" x2="70" y2="300" stroke="#d1cfc5" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
            <text class="mlabel" x="385" y="336" text-anchor="middle">test-time loop count r (log scale)</text>
            <text class="mlabel" x="26" y="175" transform="rotate(-90 26 175)" text-anchor="middle">task metric (schematic)</text>
            {[1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64].map((r) => (
              <text class="mlabel" x={rX(r)} y="316" text-anchor="middle">{r}</text>
            ))}

            <g data-tip="Recall-style curve (schematic): near its ceiling by r ≈ 8 — the shape of Huginn’s report that “HellaSwag only needs 8 recurrences” to near-saturate. Extra loops past the knee buy almost nothing." data-tip-ko="Recall류 곡선 (개략): r ≈ 8이면 천장 근처 — “HellaSwag은 8 recurrence면 충분”하다는 Huginn 보고의 형태다. 무릎을 지난 추가 loop는 거의 아무것도 사 주지 않는다.">
              <polyline class="curve-qa" points={PTS_QA}></polyline>
            </g>
            <g data-tip="Reasoning-style curve (schematic): still climbing at r = 32–64 — Huginn’s GSM8K behavior. The saturating-exponential form is Parcae’s fitted law ℒ(T) = ℒ∞ + Z·e^(−zT); its unified law also ties train-time loop count to data (exponents γ_μ ≈ 0.40, γ_D ≈ 0.78)." data-tip-ko="Reasoning류 곡선 (개략): r = 32–64에서도 상승 중 — Huginn의 GSM8K 거동. 포화 지수 형태는 Parcae의 피팅 법칙 ℒ(T) = ℒ∞ + Z·e^(−zT)이고, 통합 법칙은 train-time loop 수와 데이터를 함께 묶는다 (지수 γ_μ ≈ 0.40, γ_D ≈ 0.78).">
              <polyline class="curve-qb" points={PTS_QB}></polyline>
            </g>

            <line x1={rX(8)} y1="60" x2={rX(8)} y2="300" stroke="#141413" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4" opacity="0.5"></line>
            <g data-tip="Huginn’s zero-shot per-token early exit: stop looping when the KL divergence between successive iterations’ output distributions falls below 5×10⁻⁴ — i.e. exactly where a curve flattens. Different tokens exit at different depths." data-tip-ko="Huginn의 zero-shot per-token early exit: 연속된 iteration의 출력 분포 간 KL divergence가 5×10⁻⁴ 아래로 떨어지면 loop를 멈춘다 — 곡선이 평평해지는 바로 그 지점이다. token마다 다른 깊이에서 exit한다.">
              <rect class="sbox sbox-warm" x={rX(8) - 108} y="42" width="216" height="34" rx="8"></rect>
              <text class="ssub" x={rX(8)} y="63" text-anchor="middle">early exit: successive-iterate KL &lt; 5×10⁻⁴ (Huginn §6.1)</text>
            </g>

            <circle id="dotQA" class="dot-qa" cx={rX(8)} cy={qY(qA(8))} r="5.5"></circle>
            <circle id="dotQB" class="dot-qb" cx={rX(8)} cy={qY(qB(8))} r="5.5"></circle>
            <text class="smono" id="lblQA" x={rX(8) + 10} y={qY(qA(8)) - 8}>recall-style — saturated</text>
            <text class="smono" id="lblQB" x={rX(8) + 10} y={qY(qB(8)) + 18}>reasoning-style — climbing</text>

            <g transform="translate(90, 262)">
              <line class="curve-qa" x1="0" y1="0" x2="26" y2="0"></line>
              <text class="ssub" x="32" y="4">recall-style task (HellaSwag-like ceiling ~8)</text>
              <line class="curve-qb" x1="0" y1="18" x2="26" y2="18"></line>
              <text class="ssub" x="32" y="22">reasoning-style task (GSM8K-like, climbs to 32–64)</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="slider-row">
            <span class="smono slider-lbl">r</span>
            <input type="range" id="rSlider" min="0" max="60" value="30" aria-label="Test-time loop count" />
            <span class="smono" id="rVal">r = 8</span>
          </div>

          <p class="dt-caption" id="scaleCap"><span class="lang-en">r = 8: the recall-style curve
            has flattened — this is where per-token early exit fires — while the reasoning-style
            curve is still climbing. Depth bought this way is compute, not parameters: FLOPs scale
            linearly with r.</span><span class="lang-ko">r = 8: recall류 곡선은 평평해졌고 — 바로
            여기서 per-token early exit이 발동한다 — reasoning류 곡선은 아직 오르는 중이다. 이렇게
            산 깊이는 파라미터가 아니라 연산이다: FLOPs는 r에 선형으로 늘어난다.</span></p>

          <div class="eq-chips">
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="Huginn: zero-shot, per-token — no training change needed; the KL between successive iterates is the convergence test." data-tip-ko="Huginn: zero-shot, per-token — 학습 수정 불필요; 연속 iterate 간 KL이 수렴 판정이다.">Huginn — zero-shot KL exit</span>
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="Mixture-of-Recursions (arXiv 2507.10524) instead LEARNS per-token depth with lightweight routers — expert-choice top-k continuation, or token-choice upfront assignment." data-tip-ko="Mixture-of-Recursions (arXiv 2507.10524)는 depth를 경량 router로 학습한다 — expert-choice top-k 연장 또는 token-choice 사전 배정.">MoR — learned routers</span>
            <span class="eq-chip" data-tip="Ouro (arXiv 2510.25741) trains an entropy-regularized learned-depth objective; the released models ship total_ut_steps = 4 with an early_exit_threshold (1.0 = always full depth; the vLLM path runs all steps)." data-tip-ko="Ouro (arXiv 2510.25741)는 entropy-regularized learned-depth 목적함수로 학습; 공개 모델은 total_ut_steps = 4와 early_exit_threshold를 탑재 (1.0 = 항상 full depth; vLLM 경로는 전 스텝 실행).">Ouro — entropy-regularized depth</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Because r was sampled at training time, no single depth is baked
            in — the model must produce something sensible at r = 4 and at r = 64. That is what
            turns depth into a runtime knob: quality follows a saturating exponential in r, the
            ceiling is task-dependent (recall saturates early, reasoning keeps climbing), and a
            per-token KL test tells you when a token is done thinking. Depth becomes a scheduling
            decision, made per token, at inference. One more consequence hides inside the loop:
            every extra iteration runs attention again — which is the panel below.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">r이 학습 시점에 샘플링되었기에 특정 깊이가 구워져 있지 않다 —
            모델은 r = 4에서도 r = 64에서도 말이 되는 출력을 내야 한다. 이것이 깊이를 런타임 노브로
            바꾼다: 품질은 r의 포화 지수 곡선을 따르고, 천장은 task마다 다르며(recall은 일찍 포화,
            reasoning은 계속 상승), token이 생각을 끝냈는지는 per-token KL 검사가 알려 준다. 깊이는
            inference에서 token 단위로 내리는 스케줄링 결정이 된다. loop 안에는 결과가 하나 더 숨어
            있다: 추가 iteration마다 attention이 다시 돈다 — 그것이 아래 패널이다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <h3 class="panel-h">
            <span class="lang-en">7b · What the loop caches: KV along the iteration axis</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">7b · Loop가 cache하는 것: iteration 축의 KV</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="panel-sub">
            <span class="lang-en">Each loop iteration runs attention again, so at generation the
              naive looped decoder stores KV per (iteration × core layer) — KV grows with
              <em>effective</em> depth, not unique layers. The public Parcae cache
              (<code>parcae_lm/utils/cache.py</code>, <code>ParcaeDynamicCache</code>) keys entries
              by exactly that step index; Huginn’s fix is modulo-budget sharing.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">loop iteration마다 attention이 다시 돌기 때문에, naive looped
              decoder는 생성 시 (iteration × core layer) 단위로 KV를 저장한다 — KV는 unique layer가
              아니라 <em>유효</em> 깊이에 비례해 자란다. 공개된 Parcae cache
              (<code>parcae_lm/utils/cache.py</code>의 <code>ParcaeDynamicCache</code>)가 정확히 그
              step index로 엔트리를 keying하고, Huginn의 해법은 modulo-budget 공유다.</span>
          </p>
          <div class="mask-modes" role="group" aria-label="KV caching mode">
            <button class="mode-btn on" id="kvNaiveBtn" type="button">naive — distinct KV per iteration</button>
            <button class="mode-btn" id="kvModBtn" type="button">budget k = 4 — write slot i mod k</button>
          </div>
          <div class="loop-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 740 300" role="img" aria-label="KV cache rows along the loop axis: eight distinct per-iteration caches in naive mode, collapsing onto four shared slots under Huginn's i mod k budget" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:680px;">
            <g id="gKvNaive">
              {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7].map((i) => (
                <g data-tip={`Iteration ${i + 1} writes its own KV rows for every core layer — the default in the public Parcae cache (lookup_strategy='full', entries keyed by step_idx = recurrence step × core layer).`}
                   data-tip-ko={`Iteration ${i + 1}이 모든 core layer에 대해 자기만의 KV row를 쓴다 — 공개 Parcae cache의 기본값 (lookup_strategy='full', step_idx = recurrence step × core layer로 keying).`}>
                  <text class="smono" x="96" y={40 + i * 28 + 14} text-anchor="end">iter {i + 1}</text>
                  <rect class="kv-row" x="110" y={40 + i * 28} width="420" height="20" rx="5"></rect>
                  <text class="mlabel" x="320" y={40 + i * 28 + 14} text-anchor="middle">KV × core layers — its own copy</text>
                </g>
              ))}
              <text class="smono taccent" x="560" y="152">total: 8 × (core KV)</text>
              <text class="mlabel" x="560" y="170">grows with loop count</text>
            </g>
            <g id="gKvMod" style="display:none">
              {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((j) => (
                <g data-tip={`Shared slot ${j + 1} of k = 4: iterations ${j + 1} and ${j + 5} both read and write here (“at iteration i, read and write the cache entry i mod k” — Huginn §6.2).`}
                   data-tip-ko={`공유 slot ${j + 1} / k = 4: iteration ${j + 1}과 ${j + 5}가 여기를 함께 읽고 쓴다 (“iteration i에서 cache entry i mod k를 읽고 쓴다” — Huginn §6.2).`}>
                  <rect class="kv-row kv-shared" x="240" y={48 + j * 44} width="290" height="30" rx="6"></rect>
                  <text class="mlabel" x="385" y={48 + j * 44 + 19} text-anchor="middle">slot {j + 1} — shared KV</text>
                </g>
              ))}
              {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7].map((i) => (
                <g>
                  <text class="smono" x="96" y={40 + i * 28 + 14} text-anchor="end">iter {i + 1}</text>
                  <path class="kv-link" d={`M110,${40 + i * 28 + 10} H180 V${48 + (i % 4) * 44 + 15} H236`} fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrL)"></path>
                </g>
              ))}
              <text class="smono taccent" x="560" y="118">total: 4 × (core KV) — 2×↓ at r = 8</text>
              <text class="mlabel" x="560" y="136">“cache budget of 4: 5.86” —</text>
              <text class="mlabel" x="560" y="152">no MTBench drop (Huginn §6.2)</text>
            </g>
            <text class="ssub" x="30" y="276">related: MoR caches KV only at the recursion level a token is routed to (§2.2.2), or reuses first-recursion KV;</text>
            <text class="ssub" x="30" y="292">the public Parcae cache also ships compress-first / last / stride / anchor remaps onto earlier slots.</text>
          </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">Depth is now a per-token runtime knob — task-dependent ceilings,
            KL-based exit (&lt; 5×10⁻⁴) — but what it spends is compute: FLOPs grow linearly in r,
            and naive KV grows along the loop axis until slots are shared i mod k.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">깊이는 이제 token 단위 런타임 노브다 — task별 천장, KL 기반 exit
            (&lt; 5×10⁻⁴) — 하지만 지출되는 것은 연산이다: FLOPs는 r에 선형으로 늘고, naive KV는
            slot을 i mod k로 공유하기 전까지 loop 축을 따라 자란다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">So which resources did looping actually make cheaper? Time to open the ledger — it has four lines, and they disagree.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">그래서 looping이 실제로 싸게 만든 자원은 무엇인가? 장부를 펼 시간이다 — 네 줄이 있고, 서로 말이 다르다.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §8 · THE ACCOUNTING (DEEP WATER) ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s8">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="arc-heading"><span class="arc-num">§8</span>
          <span class="lang-en">The accounting: params ≠ FLOPs ≠ bytes</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">장부 정리: params ≠ FLOPs ≠ bytes</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">This is the hardest section of the page — take it slowly. The word
            “efficient” is doing four different jobs here: parameters, FLOPs, weight-reads, and KV
            bytes are separate ledgers, and looping moves each one differently. Everything before
            this was mechanism; this is what it costs.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">이 페이지에서 가장 어려운 섹션이다 — 천천히 읽자. 여기서
            “efficient”라는 단어는 네 가지 다른 일을 하고 있다: parameters, FLOPs, weight-read, KV
            byte는 서로 다른 장부이고, looping은 각각을 다르게 움직인다. 지금까지가 메커니즘이었다면,
            여기는 그 값이다.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Worked example, all arithmetic labeled [RE]: a 4-layer core looped
            8 times versus 32 unique layers at equal width. Four ledgers, four different
            verdicts — hover each row.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">계산 예시, 산술 전부 [RE] 표기: 동일 폭에서 4-layer core × 8 loop
            대 unique 32 layers. 장부 네 줄, 판정도 네 가지 — 각 행에 hover.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="loop-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 880 432" role="img" aria-label="Four ledgers comparing a looped 4-layer-core-times-8 model against a standard 32-layer model: unique parameter storage shrinks eight times, FLOPs and decode weight reads stay equal, and KV bytes halve only with modulo-budget sharing" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:820px;">
            {accGroups.map((g) => (
              <g data-tip={g.tipEn} data-tip-ko={g.tipKo}>
                <text class="stitle sm" x="20" y={g.y - 14}>{g.label}</text>
                {g.bars.map((b, bi) => (
                  <g>
                    <text class="smono" x="212" y={g.y + bi * 22 + 13} text-anchor="end">{b.name}</text>
                    <rect class={`acc-bar ${b.cls}`} x="220" y={g.y + bi * 22} width={b.w} height="16" rx="4"></rect>
                    {b.extra ? <rect class="acc-bar ab-extra" x={220 + b.w} y={g.y + bi * 22} width={b.extra} height="16" rx="4"></rect> : null}
                    <text class="mlabel" x={224 + b.w + (b.extra || 0)} y={g.y + bi * 22 + 12}>{b.txt}</text>
                  </g>
                ))}
                <text class="ssub" x="20" y={g.y + g.bars.length * 22 + 14}>→ {g.verdict}</text>
              </g>
            ))}
            <text class="mlabel" x="20" y="424">[RE] worked example — 4L core × 8 loops vs 32L standard, equal width d; per-layer units. Core ≈ 400 MB BF16 at d = 2048 → never SRAM-resident.</text>
          </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card-grid eff-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Where looping pays</span><span class="lang-ko">Looping이 이득인 곳</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en"><b>Storage and capacity-per-byte.</b> Looped transformers match
                standard ones on data-fitting tasks with under 10% of the parameters (arXiv
                2311.12424). <b>Test-time compute</b> without more params or longer context —
                Huginn’s r is a free knob. <b>KV, if you share it</b> along the loop axis. And
                fewer unique bytes means cheaper communication and multi-copy serving.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko"><b>저장량과 byte당 capacity.</b> looped transformer는 data-fitting
                task에서 파라미터 10% 미만으로 standard와 대등하다 (arXiv 2311.12424). 파라미터도
                context도 늘리지 않는 <b>test-time compute</b> — Huginn의 r은 공짜 노브다. loop 축으로
                공유한다면 <b>KV도</b> 이득. unique byte가 적으니 통신과 다중 복제 serving도 싸진다.</span>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Where it doesn’t</span><span class="lang-ko">이득이 아닌 곳</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en"><b>FLOPs scale with r</b> — 32 applications is 32 applications.
                <b>Batch-1 decode bandwidth</b>: the core is re-read from HBM every loop, so at
                matched effective depth the weight-read floor doesn’t drop [RE]. <b>Capacity floors
                bite at small scale</b>: MoR’s 135M model underperforms vanilla. And per-task
                ceilings saturate — more loops stop paying (§7).</span>
              <span class="lang-ko"><b>FLOPs는 r에 비례</b> — 32번 적용은 32번 적용이다.
                <b>batch-1 decode bandwidth</b>: core를 loop마다 HBM에서 다시 읽으므로, 동일 유효
                깊이에서 weight-read 바닥은 내려가지 않는다 [RE]. <b>작은 스케일에선 capacity 바닥이
                문다</b>: MoR 135M은 vanilla보다 못하다. 그리고 task별 천장이 포화하면 loop를 더 돌려도
                득이 없다 (§7).</span>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Published wins</span><span class="lang-ko">공개된 성과들</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">Parcae: “up to 6.3% lower validation perplexity over prior
                large-scale looped models”; at 1.3B, +2.99 CORE over a matched transformer — “up to
                87.5%” the relative quality of one twice its size; the 770M ≈ a 1.3B transformer on Core.
                Ouro: 1.4B/2.6B models (4 loop steps, per paper/shipped config) “match the results of up to 12B SOTA LLMs” (7.7T
                tokens). MoR-4: up to 2.06× serving throughput. LOTUS: thought-phase 2.5–6.9×
                faster than explicit CoT, 2.1× total, at ~parity accuracy.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">Parcae: “기존 대규모 looped 모델 대비 validation perplexity 최대
                6.3% 감소”; 1.3B에서 matched transformer 대비 CORE +2.99 — 2배 크기 모델의 상대 품질
                “최대 87.5%”; 770M ≈ 1.3B transformer (Core 기준). Ouro: 1.4B/2.6B(기본 4 loop steps)가 “최대 12B SOTA
                LLM에 상응하는 결과” (7.7T tokens). MoR-4: serving throughput 최대 2.06×. LOTUS:
                thought-phase가 explicit CoT보다 2.5–6.9× 빠르고, 전체 2.1×, 정확도는 ~동률.</span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              Weight tying divides <em>unique parameter storage</em> by ~r, and that is real: fewer
              bytes to hold, ship, and replicate, more capability per stored byte. But FLOPs count
              layer-<em>applications</em>, which looping does not reduce; and at batch-1 decode the
              core (hundreds of MB) is re-read from HBM every pass, so the weight-bandwidth floor at
              matched effective depth doesn’t move either [RE]. The subtlest line is KV: attention
              runs every iteration, so naive KV grows with r — until you share slots i mod k along
              the loop axis, which Huginn reports as free at budget 4.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              weight tying은 <em>unique 파라미터 저장량</em>을 ~r로 나누고, 이것은 실질적이다:
              보관·전송·복제할 byte가 줄고, 저장 byte당 능력은 커진다. 그러나 FLOPs는
              layer-<em>application</em> 수를 세고, looping은 그걸 줄이지 않는다; batch-1 decode에선
              수백 MB짜리 core를 pass마다 HBM에서 다시 읽으므로 동일 유효 깊이의 weight-bandwidth
              바닥도 움직이지 않는다 [RE]. 가장 미묘한 줄은 KV다: iteration마다 attention이 돌아
              naive KV는 r에 비례해 자란다 — loop 축에서 slot을 i mod k로 공유하기 전까지는. Huginn은
              budget 4에서 이것이 공짜라고 보고한다.
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">Params, FLOPs, weight bytes, KV bytes: four ledgers, and looping
            helps two — stored parameters (÷ ~r) and KV (only with loop-axis sharing). Compute and
            batch-1 decode weight-reads stay put at matched effective depth.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">params, FLOPs, weight bytes, KV bytes: 장부 네 줄 중 looping이 돕는
            것은 두 줄이다 — 저장 파라미터(÷ ~r)와 KV(loop 축 공유가 있을 때만). 연산량과 batch-1
            decode weight-read는 동일 유효 깊이에서 그대로다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">If the honest wins are storage, capacity-per-byte, and a brand-new KV axis — where is the field pushing next?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">정직한 이득이 저장량, byte당 capacity, 그리고 완전히 새로운 KV 축이라면 — 이 분야는 다음으로 어디를 밀고 있는가?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §9 · WHERE THIS GOES ============ -->
    <section class="section" id="arc-s9">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="arc-heading"><span class="arc-num">§9</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Where this goes</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">앞으로의 방향</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">The mechanics are on the table. What remains is the frontier: what
            the field is scaling, what it is automating, and what nobody has solved yet.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">메커니즘은 테이블 위에 다 올려놓았다. 남은 것은 최전선이다: 이
            분야가 무엇을 키우고 있고, 무엇을 자동화하고 있으며, 아직 아무도 풀지 못한 것은
            무엇인가.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">Three directions carry most of the momentum. <b>Scale</b>: Ouro
              (arXiv 2510.25741) pretrained looped LMs on 7.7T tokens, with 1.4B/2.6B models
              reported to match much larger SOTA LLMs — whether the advantage persists at frontier
              scale is open. <b>Adaptive depth</b>: Huginn exits zero-shot on a KL test,
              Mixture-of-Recursions learns per-token routers, Ouro trains an entropy-regularized
              halting objective — depth is turning into a serving and scheduling problem, and
              batching tokens that exit at different depths efficiently is largely unsolved.
              <b>The loop-axis KV cache</b>: a genuinely new structured-redundancy axis — the
              published record already spans full per-iteration caches, modulo-budget sharing, and
              recursion-wise caching — and it is an open target for cache work.</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">추진력 대부분은 세 방향에 실려 있다. <b>스케일</b>: Ouro(arXiv
              2510.25741)는 looped LM을 7.7T token으로 사전학습했고, 1.4B/2.6B 모델이 훨씬 큰 SOTA
              LLM에 상응한다고 보고한다 — frontier 스케일에서도 이 이점이 유지되는지는 열린
              문제다. <b>적응형 깊이</b>: Huginn은 KL 검사로 zero-shot exit하고,
              Mixture-of-Recursions는 token별 router를 학습하며, Ouro는 entropy-regularized
              halting 목적함수를 학습한다 — 깊이는 serving·스케줄링 문제로 변하는 중이고, 서로 다른
              깊이에서 exit하는 token들을 효율적으로 batch하는 문제는 대체로 미해결이다.
              <b>loop 축 KV cache</b>: 진짜로 새로운 구조적 중복 축이다 — 공개된 기록만 해도 full
              per-iteration cache, modulo-budget 공유, recursion-wise caching에 걸쳐 있다 — cache
              연구의 열린 표적이다.</span>
          </p>
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">Two edges are worth watching from this site’s reviews: LOTUS uses
              the loop to bridge latent and explicit chain-of-thought reasoning
              (<a href="/reviews/lotus/">review</a>), and at the small-model end weight sharing is
              already shipping — MobileLLM’s block-wise layer sharing is the same trick aimed at
              on-device budgets (<a href="/reviews/mobilellm/">review</a>).</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">이 사이트의 리뷰에서 지켜볼 만한 가장자리 둘: LOTUS는 loop로
              latent reasoning과 explicit chain-of-thought 사이를 잇고
              (<a href="/reviews/lotus/">리뷰</a>), 소형 모델 쪽에서는 weight 공유가 이미 제품으로
              나가고 있다 — MobileLLM의 block-wise layer 공유는 같은 트릭을 on-device 예산에 겨눈
              것이다 (<a href="/reviews/mobilellm/">리뷰</a>).</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="eff-note band-dark">
          <h3>
            <span class="lang-en">Why this matters for efficiency work</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">효율화 연구에 왜 중요한가</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            <span class="lang-en">
              Looped models redraw the serving map. First, they create a <em>new cache axis</em>:
              KV per loop iteration, which is exactly the kind of structured redundancy compression
              lives on — the published record already spans full per-iteration caches, modulo-budget
              sharing, and routed recursion-wise caching. Second, they decouple the knobs: a model’s
              quality can now be spent or saved per token at serve time (early exit), which turns
              accelerator questions into scheduling questions. Third, they are honest about what
              weight tying cannot buy — the decode weight-read floor stays put at matched depth, so
              the interesting seams are where r is adaptive, batched, or amortized. That is the
              lens this site keeps applying: find where the bytes actually move.
            </span>
            <span class="lang-ko">
              looped 모델은 serving 지도를 다시 그린다. 첫째, <em>새로운 cache 축</em>을 만든다:
              loop iteration별 KV — compression이 먹고 사는 바로 그 구조적 중복이며, 공개된 기록만
              해도 full per-iteration cache, modulo-budget 공유, routing 기반 recursion-wise
              caching까지 걸쳐 있다. 둘째, 노브를 분리한다: 모델 품질을 serve 시점에 token 단위로
              쓰거나 아낄 수 있게 되면서(early exit), 가속 문제가 스케줄링 문제로 바뀐다. 셋째,
              weight tying이 사 줄 수 없는 것에 정직하다 — 동일 깊이에서 decode weight-read 바닥은
