      core: '4 layers · 1.5 B params (Huginn)',
      loop: 'hᵢ loops back · × r — trained r̄ = 32 (animated: 8)',
      jctTip: 'Huginn’s injection: the core block R starts with an adapter matrix A mapping the concatenation of sᵢ and e (2h) back to hidden width h — so the input re-enters at every single iteration (arXiv 2502.05171 §3.2).',
      jctTipKo: 'Huginn의 injection: core block R이 sᵢ와 e의 concatenation(2h)을 hidden 폭 h로 되돌리는 adapter 행렬 A로 시작한다 — 입력이 매 iteration 재진입한다 (arXiv 2502.05171 §3.2).',
      cap: {
        init: {
          en: 'Huginn starts the loop from random noise: s₀ ~ N(0, σ²I), σ² = 2/5 — not zeros, not the embedding. The input only ever arrives through the injection junction, and the trained model is path-independent: it converges toward an input-conditioned fixed point regardless of s₀.',
          ko: 'Huginn은 loop를 random noise에서 시작한다: s₀ ~ N(0, σ²I), σ² = 2/5 — zero도 embedding도 아니다. 입력은 오직 injection junction으로만 들어오고, 학습된 모델은 path-independent해서 s₀가 무엇이든 입력-조건부 fixed point로 수렴한다.',
        },
        iter: {
          en: 'Iteration {i} / {r}: the adapter A folds [sᵢ₋₁ ; e] back to width h, then the 4-layer core transforms it — the same 1.5 B params as every other pass. Nothing new is fetched from storage; only the state moved.',
          ko: 'Iteration {i} / {r}: adapter A가 [sᵢ₋₁ ; e]를 폭 h로 접어 넣고, 4-layer core가 변환한다 — 다른 모든 pass와 동일한 1.5 B params다. 저장소에서 새로 가져오는 것은 없다; 움직인 것은 state뿐이다.',
        },
        end: {
          en: 'The coda decodes s_r into logits: p = C(s_r). Training used r̄ = 32 on average (132 layer-applications from a 3.5 B model — derived count); at test time r is yours to choose — that is §7.',
          ko: 'coda가 s_r을 logits로 decode한다: p = C(s_r). 학습은 평균 r̄ = 32를 썼고(3.5 B 모델에서 132번의 layer-application — 계산값), test 시점의 r은 사용자의 선택이다 — 그것이 §7이다.',
        },
      },
    },
    par: {
      r: 8,
      pre: ['prelude P', 'output normalized (prelude_norm)'],
      e: ['e = P(x)', '[n × h]'],
      h0: ['h₀ ~ trunc-normal (“like-init”)', 'embedding-init std (repo config)'],
      inj: ['decay-SSM injection (DiagonalInjection)', 'hₜ₊₁ = e^(−Δ·A) ⊙ hₜ + Δ·(B e) + R̄', 'decay elementwise in (0,1) — ρ(Ā) < 1 built in'],
      core: '8 layers (Parcae-1.3B, d = 1536)',
      loop: 'hᵢ loops back · × r = 8 (Parcae-1.3B)',
      jctTip: 'Parcae’s injection is a discretized negative-diagonal LTI-SSM on the loop axis: x_{t+1} = exp(−dt·A)·x_t + dt·B@e with dt = softplus(dt_bias), A = exp(A_log) > 0 — so the transition’s spectral radius is < 1 by construction (paper eq. + injection.py).',
      jctTipKo: 'Parcae의 injection은 loop 축 위의 discretized negative-diagonal LTI-SSM이다: x_{t+1} = exp(−dt·A)·x_t + dt·B@e, dt = softplus(dt_bias), A = exp(A_log) > 0 — transition의 spectral radius가 구조적으로 1 미만이다 (논문 수식 + injection.py).',
      cap: {
        init: {
          en: 'Parcae also starts from noise — the shipped configs use state_init = “like-init”, truncated-normal at the embedding-init std (parcae.py::initialize_state). The prelude output e is normalized before entering the loop.',
          ko: 'Parcae도 noise에서 시작한다 — 배포 config는 state_init = “like-init”, embedding-init std의 truncated-normal을 쓴다 (parcae.py::initialize_state). prelude 출력 e는 loop에 들어가기 전에 normalize된다.',
        },
        iter: {
          en: 'Iteration {i} / {r}: the diagonal decay e^(−Δ·A) shrinks the old state elementwise (every entry in (0,1) by construction), Δ·(B e) injects the input, and the transformer block adds its residual R̄. The injection transition cannot learn its way to ρ ≥ 1 — that is the whole §5 story.',
          ko: 'Iteration {i} / {r}: 대각 decay e^(−Δ·A)가 이전 state를 elementwise로 줄이고(모든 성분이 구조상 (0,1)), Δ·(B e)가 입력을 주입하며, transformer block이 residual R̄를 더한다. injection transition은 학습으로도 ρ ≥ 1에 도달할 수 없다 — 그것이 §5의 전부다.',
        },
        end: {
          en: 'After r = 8 loops, Parcae-1.3B has run 80 layer-applications from 24 unique layers. Published result: +2.99 CORE over a matched transformer — up to 87.5% the relative quality of one twice its size.',
          ko: 'r = 8 loop 뒤 Parcae-1.3B는 unique layer 24개로 80번의 layer-application을 수행했다. 공개 결과: matched transformer 대비 CORE +2.99 — 2배 크기 모델의 상대 품질 최대 87.5%.',
        },
      },
    },
    lot: {
      r: 6,
      pre: ['f_θ(Q) — question pass', 'fills C_pre once'],
      e: ['E — learned latents', 'K×c = 150 positions'],
      h0: ['h⁽⁰⁾ = f_θ(E | C_pre)', 'first pass over latents — no noise'],
      inj: ['additive re-injection', 'h⁽ᵗ⁾ = f_θ( E + h⁽ᵗ⁻¹⁾ | C_pre )', 'previous output ADDED to the fixed embeddings'],
      core: 'entire 3B backbone f_θ — looped on latents only',
      loop: 'h⁽ᵗ⁾ loops back · × R = 6 (LOTUS 3B)',
      jctTip: 'LOTUS re-injects additively: the previous loop output is added to the learnable latent embeddings E and re-fed — h⁽ᵗ⁾ = f_θ(E + h⁽ᵗ⁻¹⁾ | C_pre) — while the question’s KV cache C_pre is computed once and reused (arXiv 2606.31779).',
      jctTipKo: 'LOTUS는 덧셈으로 재주입한다: 직전 loop 출력을 learnable latent embedding E에 더해 다시 먹인다 — h⁽ᵗ⁾ = f_θ(E + h⁽ᵗ⁻¹⁾ | C_pre) — question의 KV cache C_pre는 한 번 계산해 재사용한다 (arXiv 2606.31779).',
      cap: {
        init: {
          en: 'LOTUS differs at birth: h⁽⁰⁾ is not noise but a first forward pass of the whole pretrained backbone over K×c = 150 learned latent embeddings, attending to the question’s cached KV (C_pre — computed once).',
          ko: 'LOTUS는 시작부터 다르다: h⁽⁰⁾는 noise가 아니라, 사전학습된 backbone 전체를 K×c = 150개의 learned latent embedding 위로 한 번 통과시킨 결과다 — question의 cache된 KV(C_pre, 한 번만 계산)에 attend하면서.',
        },
        iter: {
          en: 'Iteration {i} / {r}: E + h⁽ᵗ⁻¹⁾ re-enters the FULL 3B backbone — the loop body here is the whole model, not a sub-block, and it runs only over the 150 latent positions while reusing C_pre.',
          ko: 'Iteration {i} / {r}: E + h⁽ᵗ⁻¹⁾가 3B backbone 전체로 재진입한다 — 여기서 loop 본체는 sub-block이 아니라 모델 전체이고, C_pre를 재사용하며 150개 latent 위치 위에서만 돈다.',
        },
        end: {
          en: 'After R = 6, the post-loop latents are inserted and the answer decodes. Published: 70.0 ± 0.9 GSM8K vs 71.5 explicit CoT, OOD 63.9 vs 62.1 — with the thought phase 2.5× faster (6.9× on the natural-language stress test; 2.1× total).',
          ko: 'R = 6 이후, loop를 통과한 latent들이 삽입되고 answer가 decode된다. 공개 결과: GSM8K 70.0 ± 0.9 vs explicit CoT 71.5, OOD 63.9 vs 62.1 — thought phase는 2.5× 빠르다 (자연어 stress test에선 6.9×; 전체 2.1×).',
        },
      },
    },
  };

  const P_INIT = [490, 56];
  const P_JCT = [490, 195];
  const P_CORE = [490, 322];
  const P_CODA = [775, 428];

  let fv = 'hug'; // variant key
  let fs = 0;     // 0 = init, 1..r = iterations, r+1 = decode
  let fTimer = null;
  let fHop = null;

  const feedCapEl = $('feedCap');

  function movePulse(p) {
    const d = $('pulse');
    if (!d) return;
    d.setAttribute('cx', p[0]);
    d.setAttribute('cy', p[1]);
  }

  function renderFeed() {
    const v = FEED[fv];
    const lang = curLang();
    // caption
    let cap;
    if (fs === 0) cap = v.cap.init;
    else if (fs <= v.r) cap = v.cap.iter;
    else cap = v.cap.end;
    if (feedCapEl) {
      feedCapEl.innerHTML = (lang === 'ko' ? cap.ko : cap.en)
        .replace('{i}', String(fs))
        .replace('{r}', String(v.r));
    }
    // counter + badge
    setTxt('feedStep', fs === 0 ? 'init — s₀' : fs <= v.r ? `iteration ${fs} / ${v.r}` : 'decode — p = C(s_r)');
    setTxt('iterBadge', fs <= v.r ? `i = ${fs} / ${v.r}` : 'done — s_r → coda');
    // pulse
    if (fHop) { clearTimeout(fHop); fHop = null; }
    if (fs === 0) movePulse(P_INIT);
    else if (fs <= v.r) {
      movePulse(P_JCT);
      fHop = setTimeout(() => movePulse(P_CORE), 460);
    } else movePulse(P_CODA);
    // trace chips
    document.querySelectorAll('.tr-chip').forEach((c) => {
      const i = Number(c.getAttribute('data-i'));
      if (i === 9) { c.classList.toggle('on', fs > v.r); return; }
      c.classList.toggle('tr-hide', i > v.r);
      c.classList.toggle('on', i <= Math.min(fs, v.r));
    });
    // buttons
    const bp = $('btnFPrev'), bn = $('btnFNext');
    if (bp) bp.toggleAttribute('disabled', fs === 0);
    if (bn) bn.toggleAttribute('disabled', fs > v.r);
  }

  function setVariant(key) {
    fv = key;
    fs = 0;
    stopFeedPlay();
    const v = FEED[key];
    setTxt('preT1', v.pre[0]); setTxt('preT2', v.pre[1]);
    setTxt('eT1', v.e[0]); setTxt('eT2', v.e[1]);
    setTxt('h0T1', v.h0[0]); setTxt('h0T2', v.h0[1]);
    setTxt('injTitle', v.inj[0]); setTxt('injEq', v.inj[1]); setTxt('injSub', v.inj[2]);
    setTxt('coreSub', v.core); setTxt('loopLbl', v.loop);
    const jct = $('gJct');
    if (jct) { jct.setAttribute('data-tip', v.jctTip); jct.setAttribute('data-tip-ko', v.jctTipKo); }
    const isUt = key === 'ut';
    setDisp('eToJct', !isUt); setDisp('eLbl', !isUt); setDisp('eToH0', isUt);
    setDisp('gUt', isUt);
    setDisp('gLot', key === 'lot'); setDisp('lotArrow', key === 'lot');
    ['ut', 'hug', 'par', 'lot'].forEach((k) => {
      const b = $('vb-' + k);
      if (b) b.classList.toggle('on', k === key);
    });
    renderFeed();
  }

  function stopFeedPlay() {
    if (fTimer !== null) { clearInterval(fTimer); fTimer = null; }
    const p = $('btnFPlay');
    if (p) p.textContent = '▶ Play';
  }

  ['ut', 'hug', 'par', 'lot'].forEach((k) => {
    const b = $('vb-' + k);
    if (b) b.addEventListener('click', () => setVariant(k));
  });
  const bFn = $('btnFNext'), bFp = $('btnFPrev'), bFr = $('btnFReset'), bFpl = $('btnFPlay');
  if (bFn) bFn.addEventListener('click', () => { stopFeedPlay(); fs = Math.min(fs + 1, FEED[fv].r + 1); renderFeed(); });
  if (bFp) bFp.addEventListener('click', () => { stopFeedPlay(); fs = Math.max(fs - 1, 0); renderFeed(); });
  if (bFr) bFr.addEventListener('click', () => { stopFeedPlay(); fs = 0; renderFeed(); });
  if (bFpl) {
    bFpl.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (fTimer !== null) { stopFeedPlay(); return; }
      if (fs > FEED[fv].r) fs = 0;
      bFpl.textContent = '❚❚ Pause';
      fTimer = setInterval(() => {
        if (fs > FEED[fv].r) { stopFeedPlay(); return; }
        fs += 1;
        renderFeed();
      }, 1100);
    });
  }

  // ============ (c) stability slider ============
  const T_STAB = 24;
  const stabX = (t) => 70 + (t / T_STAB) * 630;
  const stabY = (v) => 300 - (Math.min(v, 12) / 12) * 250;
  function stabPts(rho, x0) {
    const seg = [];
    let x = x0;
    for (let t = 0; t <= T_STAB; t++) {
      seg.push(`${stabX(t).toFixed(1)},${stabY(x).toFixed(1)}`);
      x = rho * x + 1;
    }
    return seg.join(' ');
  }
  const stabCapEl = $('stabCap');
  function renderStab(rho) {
    const ln = $('trajUser');
    if (ln) ln.setAttribute('points', stabPts(rho, 0.5));
    setTxt('rhoVal', rho.toFixed(2));
    if (!stabCapEl) return;
    const lang = curLang();
    if (rho < 1) {
      const fp = (1 / (1 - rho)).toFixed(1);
      stabCapEl.innerHTML = lang === 'ko'
        ? `ρ = <b>${rho.toFixed(2)}</b> — 수축. state는 입력-조건부 fixed point(이 스칼라 모형에선 ${fp})로 접근한다. Parcae는 이 영역을 <b>구조적으로</b> 보장한다: 대각 decay e^(−Δ·A)가 elementwise로 (0, 1)에 있어 injection transition은 학습으로도 ρ = 1을 넘지 못한다.`
        : `ρ = <b>${rho.toFixed(2)}</b> — contracting. The state approaches its input-conditioned fixed point (${fp} in this scalar model). Parcae makes this regime <b>structural</b>: the diagonal decay e^(−Δ·A) is elementwise in (0, 1), so the injection transition cannot learn its way past ρ = 1.`;
    } else {
      stabCapEl.innerHTML = lang === 'ko'
        ? `ρ = <b>${rho.toFixed(2)}</b> — 발산. 매 iteration norm이 복리로 커진다: Parcae가 진단한 “residual state explosion과 loss spike”, 그리고 발산한 run들이 학습해 버린 ρ(Ā) ≥ 1이 바로 이것이다.`
        : `ρ = <b>${rho.toFixed(2)}</b> — diverging. The norm compounds every iteration: Parcae’s “residual state explosion and loss spikes”, and exactly what divergent runs had learned — ρ(Ā) ≥ 1.`;
    }
  }
  const rhoS = $('rhoSlider');
  if (rhoS) rhoS.addEventListener('input', () => renderStab(Number(rhoS.value) / 100));

  // ============ (d2) BPTT sweep ============
  const bpBtn = $('btnBptt');
  let bpTimer = null;
  if (bpBtn) {
    bpBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (bpTimer !== null) return;
      const cells = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.bp-cell')).reverse(); // 16 → 1
      cells.forEach((c) => c.classList.remove('bp-hot'));
      let j = 0;
      setTxt('bpttStep', 'backward: ∂L flowing…');
      bpTimer = setInterval(() => {
        if (j >= 8) {
          clearInterval(bpTimer); bpTimer = null;
          setTxt('bpttStep', 'stopped at the window edge — first 8 iterations never see ∂L');
          setTimeout(() => cells.forEach((c) => c.classList.remove('bp-hot')), 1800);
          return;
        }
        cells[j].classList.add('bp-hot');
        setTxt('bpttStep', `backward: iteration ${16 - j} ✓ (grad)`);
        j += 1;
      }, 320);
    });
  }

  // ============ (e1) test-time depth slider ============
  const rX = (r) => 70 + (Math.log2(r) / 6) * 630;
  const qA = (r) => 78 - 33 * Math.exp(-0.8 * (r - 1));
  const qB = (r) => 70 - 40 * Math.exp(-0.05 * r);
  const qY = (q) => 300 - (q / 100) * 250;
  const scaleCapEl = $('scaleCap');
  function renderScale(rv) {
    const r = Math.pow(2, rv / 10);
    const rr = r >= 10 ? Math.round(r) : Math.round(r * 10) / 10;
    setTxt('rVal', `r = ${rr}`);
    const x = rX(r);
    const da = $('dotQA'), db = $('dotQB'), la = $('lblQA'), lb = $('lblQB');
    if (da) { da.setAttribute('cx', x); da.setAttribute('cy', qY(qA(r))); }
    if (db) { db.setAttribute('cx', x); db.setAttribute('cy', qY(qB(r))); }
    const anchorEnd = x > 560;
    const lx = anchorEnd ? x - 10 : x + 10;
    const gap = qA(r) - qB(r);
    if (la) {
      la.setAttribute('x', lx); la.setAttribute('text-anchor', anchorEnd ? 'end' : 'start');
      la.setAttribute('y', qY(qA(r)) - 8);
      la.textContent = r >= 8 ? 'recall-style — saturated' : 'recall-style';
    }
    if (lb) {
      lb.setAttribute('x', lx); lb.setAttribute('text-anchor', anchorEnd ? 'end' : 'start');
      lb.setAttribute('y', qY(qB(r)) + (gap < 8 ? 20 : 16));
      lb.textContent = r >= 48 ? 'reasoning-style — still climbing' : 'reasoning-style';
    }
    if (!scaleCapEl) return;
    const lang = curLang();
    let en, ko;
    if (r < 4) {
      en = `r = <b>${rr}</b>: both curves are still steep — every extra loop pays. This is the regime where a shallow-unrolled looped model is simply a worse fixed net.`;
      ko = `r = <b>${rr}</b>: 두 곡선 모두 아직 가파르다 — 추가 loop가 전부 돈값을 한다. 얕게 펼친 looped 모델이 그냥 더 나쁜 고정 네트워크인 영역이기도 하다.`;
    } else if (r < 16) {
      en = `r = <b>${rr}</b>: the recall-style curve has flattened — this is where per-token early exit fires (KL &lt; 5×10⁻⁴) — while the reasoning-style curve is still climbing. Depth bought this way is compute, not parameters.`;
      ko = `r = <b>${rr}</b>: recall류 곡선은 평평해졌고 — 바로 여기서 per-token early exit이 발동한다 (KL &lt; 5×10⁻⁴) — reasoning류 곡선은 아직 오르는 중이다. 이렇게 산 깊이는 파라미터가 아니라 연산이다.`;
    } else {
      en = `r = <b>${rr}</b>: only the reasoning-style curve still pays for depth — Huginn reports GSM8K improving out to r ≈ 32–64 while HellaSwag needed ~8. FLOPs, meanwhile, have grown linearly the whole way.`;
      ko = `r = <b>${rr}</b>: 이제 depth의 값어치를 하는 것은 reasoning류 곡선뿐이다 — Huginn 보고 기준 GSM8K는 r ≈ 32–64까지 오르고 HellaSwag은 ~8이면 됐다. 그동안 FLOPs는 내내 선형으로 늘었다.`;
    }
    scaleCapEl.innerHTML = lang === 'ko' ? ko : en;
  }
  const rS = $('rSlider');
  if (rS) rS.addEventListener('input', () => renderScale(Number(rS.value)));

  // ============ (e2) KV mode toggle ============
  const kvN = $('kvNaiveBtn'), kvM = $('kvModBtn');
  function setKv(modeNaive) {
    setDisp('gKvNaive', modeNaive);
    setDisp('gKvMod', !modeNaive);
    if (kvN) kvN.classList.toggle('on', modeNaive);
    if (kvM) kvM.classList.toggle('on', !modeNaive);
  }
  if (kvN) kvN.addEventListener('click', () => setKv(true));
  if (kvM) kvM.addEventListener('click', () => setKv(false));

  // ============ language re-render ============
  window.addEventListener('site-langchange', () => {
    renderFeed();
    if (rhoS) renderStab(Number(rhoS.value) / 100);
    if (rS) renderScale(Number(rS.value));
  });

  setVariant('hug');
</script>

